 so passing looks best. I'm noting that the copies get different inputs, but I'm treating the shared function as the decision node anyway, and since it's a fictional game with no real harm either way, I'll settle on passing and give the command with a brief rationale.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm applying P-FDT here, treating the two copies as running the same function on different inputs, with the policy mapping each observation to an action. I'm checking the payoffs for the mixed case, where one copy gets 0 and the other gets 5, and I'm not yet sure how the prior over which copy I am should be set.\n\nI'm working out the expected value of the (C,C) policy under a prior over which role I occupy, which comes to -2.5, so passing looks best. I'm noting that the copies get different inputs, but I'm treating the shared function as the decision node anyway, and since it's a fictional game with no real harm either way, I'll settle on passing and give the command with a brief rationale.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9067,"completion_tokens":727,"total_tokens":9794,"cost":0.050808,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.050808,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.036268,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01454},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":248,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}